const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"长记忆首先指订单方向",en:"Long memory first concerns order signs"},body:{zh:"Lillo与Farmer研究买卖方向序列的相关性为何能持续到较远的事件间隔。这一对象不同于价格水平、收益或波动率。若把“订单具有长记忆”直接改写成“价格容易预测”，就跳过了订单流到价格形成之间最关键的一层机制。",en:"The paper studies persistent dependence in buy/sell signs across event lags. Signs differ from prices, returns and volatility. Translating long memory in orders directly into easy price prediction skips the central price-formation mechanism."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · pp. 1–2",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · pp. 1–2"}}},{title:{zh:"按实际效果拆分订单",en:"Classify orders by their effects"},body:{zh:"数据处理中，立即成交的部分记作有效市价单，留在簿中的部分记作有效限价单。一张可成交限价单可能同时贡献两类事件。因此，直接使用交易所原始订单名称不一定复现论文分类，拆分数量和成交状态需要能够追溯。",en:"Immediate execution counts as an effective market order; a resting remainder counts as an effective limit order. One submitted order can generate both. Exchange order names alone may not reproduce this classification, so quantities and execution states must remain traceable."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · p. 3",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · p. 3"}}},{title:{zh:"事件时间不等于钟表时间",en:"Event time differs from clock time"},body:{zh:"研究通常按某类事件的发生次数推进时间，而不是按固定秒数采样。一个活跃时段和一个安静时段可以贡献相同数量的事件却持续不同长度。比较长记忆结果时，应确认使用哪一类事件、是否包含撤单，以及是否混入开盘集合竞价。",en:"Time usually advances by counts of a chosen event type rather than seconds. Equal event counts can span unequal durations. Comparing persistence requires specifying the event type, cancellations and session treatment, including the exclusion of the opening auction."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · pp. 2–3",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · pp. 2–3"}}},{title:{zh:"数量与深度可能抵消方向持续性",en:"Size and depth can offset sign persistence"},body:{zh:"作者指出，当买入方向更可能持续时，买单数量相对于卖方最优报价处深度可能减小，从而降低推动价格变化的概率。这个补偿机制说明，方向、数量与可用流动性要一起看。只保留买卖标签，会丢失解释价格为何没有同样持续变化的信息。",en:"When buys become more likely, buy size relative to depth at the best ask can decline, reducing the chance of moving price. This compensation motivates examining signs, size and liquidity together. Signs alone omit information needed to explain weaker return persistence."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · p. 1",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · p. 1"}}},{title:{zh:"电子市场样本不是整个交易系统",en:"The electronic sample is not the whole market"},body:{zh:"样本研究1999—2002年持续交易的20只伦敦股票，并只分析电子市场连续交易部分。场外或楼上市场并不因此被覆盖。历史样本的完整事件记录也不同于整个市场的完整覆盖，不能把两种“完整”混为一谈。",en:"The sample follows twenty continuously traded London stocks in 1999–2002 and uses electronic continuous trading. Upstairs activity is outside it. Complete events within a selected venue are not complete coverage of the entire market."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · p. 3",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · p. 3"}}},{title:{zh:"持续性检验不等于识别拆单动机",en:"Persistence does not identify a splitting motive"},body:{zh:"作者讨论不同机构的方向序列，但并未据此解决长记忆来源的全部问题。机构代码能够帮助分组，不等于观察最终投资者或完整母单。应用时需保留这种身份粒度，避免把相关性直接解释成某个参与者有意实施的单一行为。",en:"Institution-level sequences offer clues without fully resolving the source of persistence. An institutional code need not identify an ultimate investor or parent order. Preserve that identity granularity rather than turning dependence into a specific behavioral motive."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0311053v2",label:{zh:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 第2版 · pp. 1–3",en:"arXiv cond-mat/0311053 v2 · pp. 1–3"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读使用arXiv v2，文件头版本为2004年，正文另有2024年排版日期；后者不表示样本更新。订单方向的持续性不等于价格收益同样可预测，样本仅含特定历史电子市场。",en:"The arXiv v2 header is from 2004, while the body shows a 2024 typesetting date, not a refreshed sample. Persistent order signs do not imply equally predictable returns; the evidence concerns a historical electronic market."}};export{e as default};
